From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Razoc <razoc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:48:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 38/51] feat(akibot): DLSS and frame generation on game version
 01.007.000

Astro Bot 01.007.000 has another temporal upscale pass (pixel shader
5a34b303576ee324, layout B) than 01.019.000 (2936e5eca99d75e7), so DLSS
Super Resolution never replaced it and frame generation never got its
camera constants ("missing common constants" on every frame).

- ReadPass() reads either layout: B has the output and input sizes at
  dwords 0-3, the frame at 7, motion vectors used at 9; its images are
  colour, motion vectors (the G-buffer target, found by its recorded
  depth attachment) and history.
- Layout B has no jitter in its constants: it is taken from the game's
  jittered projection (third column, m[8] and m[9]) seen by
  NoteFrameGenCamera, which now also runs for DLSS alone.
- AKIBOT_DLSS_PASS_B overrides the second hash.
- DLSS presets: AKIBOT_DLSS_QUALITY=ultra (Ultra Performance).

Checked in Sky Garden: DLSS 1920x1080 -> 2432x1368 on every frame,
picture clean; frame generation 4.00 frames shown per game frame
(39 game FPS, 156 on screen), tags on every frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
